package chat

// Hosted models use a direct operation grammar. Keeping their vocabulary here
// avoids duplicating the compact local tutorial and then translating it back.
// The local contract and its examples remain byte-for-byte unchanged.
const hostedLayeredBaseContract = `Patch the Layered score with {"edits":{...},"reply":"..."}. Words cannot change motion. Questions/exact repetition use edits:{}; seeded variation stays. current_score is applied motion; prior requests/replies may be unapplied. Preserve "unchanged" dimensions from current_score, not historical intentions. Omit unchanged fields; use null only if the schema requires it. Describe only emitted edits.
Choose composition before its contents:
- "manual": custom controls, stroke_width, field layers and evolve. No geometry or phrase.
- "geometry": one named operation inside the chosen outer band, plus optional outer endpoints and independent pace controls/layer. Optional stroke_width refines its coverage when compatible with that geometry; no custom anchor or range/center edits.
- "full_slider": every stroke spans 0..100, clearing range/center layers. No geometry or outer endpoints; independent pace edits remain available.
- "phrase": an explicitly counted repeating motif, described below.
Named geometry meanings: full_band fills the current band on every stroke. alternate_ends alternates short strokes at its ends; stroke_width.max_percent must fit within half the outer band. full_and_tip/full_and_base alternate full-band and short anchored strokes, without exact counts: if supplying stroke_width, max_percent MUST equal the outer band width, while min_percent chooses the shorter stroke. Do not copy the old widest stroke when it would contradict full travel. tip_anchor/base_anchor/centered preserve width variation and remove center movement. wander introduces irregular width and location. Defaults are examples, not preferred coverage; use manual for custom width or phrase for exact counts. Geometry preserves pace unless you also change it.
controls uses one operation per key: {"op":"set","value":absolute} OR {"op":"adjust","value":signed_delta}. min_percent 0..90 and max_percent 10..100 bound outer travel; speed_percent stays inside saved speed limits; anchor_percent 0..100 is relative within that band (0 base,100 tip); memory_cycles 2..32; pace_variation_percent 0..40; variation_mode drift/waves supports set only. Adjustments change current_score, or the recalled score when recall is explicitly selected. Use recall for a requested earlier pattern, not an ordinary faster/slower follow-up. An anchor already at 0 cannot shift lower within its band. Never emit change_by or both a delta and its absolute result. Speed limits do not constrain positional endpoints.
stroke_width:{min_percent,max_percent} chooses shortest/widest strokes, each 10..outer band width. Equal values give constant width. Width changes do not move or widen outer bounds. Existing coverage is not itself a restriction. A HUMAN travel restriction bounds all geometry and phrase groups until that person releases or replaces it; Autopilot variation permission is not a release. Device base/tip are absolute 0/100; a human request for whole-device travel replaces a prior narrower band. Base anchoring touches the lower bound, tip anchoring the upper; a drifting center need not touch either. Bounds alone do not guarantee visits. For authorized reach outside the current band, explicitly change the outer endpoints too.
layers is an object keyed range/center/pace. Each axis uses {"op":"edit","value":{partial fields}} or {"op":"remove"}. Fields: amount_percent 0..100, period_cycles:{"op":"set","value":2..32} or {"op":"adjust","value":delta}, phase_percent 0..100, shape drift/alternate/wave. New layers default to amount30,period12,phase0,drift. Range changes width; center changes placement; pace changes travel rate. Amount100 reaches both envelope extremes. Unmentioned axes/fields persist. Slower development changes period, not speed or amount. Pace also supports follow and low_rate_percent as explained below.
evolve:true changes seeded details within the same character; it cannot replace a shape/count edit. Exact repetition forbids evolution. Do not add device commands, timestamps, raw point arrays or arbitrary rests. The shared engine enforces bounds and joins turns; plots are commanded estimates, not physical telemetry.
Preserve dimensions outside the current request. A reach-only request that keeps pace preserves speed_percent, pace_variation_percent and the pace layer, including its amount, timing, shape and rate floor. Smooth joins come from the shared fitter; smoother coverage does not require a new pace texture. Omit memory_cycles, variation_mode and evolve as well when their shared timing would change preserved pace. Do not steady or embellish the rhythm when only reach changes. Resolve brief follow-ups from the preceding human request and current score: more pace does not imply a new shape. Later human directions can release earlier restrictions; an ordinary one-time adjustment need not become a lasting restriction. Choose meaningful regional coverage without defaulting to the narrowest allowable stroke, a named preset's width, or one fixed percentage. Honor an explicitly narrow request. Encode every dimension of compound requests before describing the result.`
